  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Atlantic Diving Supply recorded $3.2B in contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Atlantic Diving Supply won 50,952 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $63.2K. Atlantic Diving Supply obligations are down 46.3% year over year. Historical obligations show a rise from $2.9B in FY21 to $6B in FY25, then a decline to $3.2B in FY26. The Department of Defense is the dominant buyer in FY2026 to date with $3.1B in obligations. The General Services Administration is the next largest buyer with $84.4M, followed by the Department of Homeland Security with $23.1M and the Department of State with $21.2M. Service Establishment Equipment and Supplies Merchant Wholesalers is the largest NAICS market for Atlantic Diving Supply with $1.9B in obligations, followed by All Other Miscellaneous Manufacturing at $950M and Bare Printed Circuit Board Manufacturing at $105M. Current-year totals are partial, reflecting fiscal year to date reporting rather than full-year results.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are the top buyers of Atlantic Diving Supply in FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $3.1B to Atlantic Diving Supply in FY2026 to date. The General Services Administration obligated $84.4M, the Department of Homeland Security obligated $23.1M, and the Department of State obligated $21.2M. Smaller federal buyers include the Department of Justice with $7.2M and the Department of Energy with $1.2M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What markets and product lines drive Atlantic Diving Supply obligations?",
        "body": "Service Establishment Equipment and Supplies Merchant Wholesalers accounts for $1.9B of obligations in FY2026 to date. All Other Miscellaneous Manufacturing accounts for $950M, and Bare Printed Circuit Board Manufacturing accounts for $105M. Additional markets include All Other Miscellaneous Fabricated Metal Product Manufacturing at $62.3M and Military Armored Vehicle, Tank, and Tank Component Manufacturing at $37.2M."
      }
    ]
